      ":question/problem": "Plot the graph of $y=4^{x}-1.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we plot the graph of $y=4^{x}{:}$\n\n![](images/df/dfac014ecedaa03a46048b4729ddfa60e7a3776322d0b9ea19035fbcd24bf85b.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y=4^x-1,$ we take the graph of $y=4^x$ and shift it $1$ unit down. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,0),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-1.$\n\n![](images/ee/eef6c5dd67c683ccd0826caa9760fa240be973f8debd29b41d463f6184a00620.png)"
    },
